      "arguments": "{\"reason\":\"All failed generations share the same verbose 'Here's a thinking process' opening. Test whether this boilerplate trajectory is the attractor: remove only the fixed output direction favoring 'Here' over a direct 'We' calculation opening, without changing decoding settings.\",\"code\":\"print('opening tokens',[(s,[int(x) for x in tokenize(s)]) for s in ['Here','We','Thinking']])\\nopening=(emb[int(tokenize('Here')[0])]-emb[int(tokenize('We')[0])])*(1+fnorm)\\nopening=opening/np.linalg.norm(opening)\\nclear_edits()\\nfor n in writers:\\n    w=weight(n)\\n    save_edit(n,w-np.outer(opening,opening@w))\\ncheckpoint('boilerplate_opening_ablation')\\nprint('One fixed lexical opening direction removed from residual writers.')\"}",
